# What every reader of fixtures/proj4.log.store must answer (LV-INC-A, PROJ kind 3 = BLOB; crates/bebop-store/src/proj/kinds.rs).
# The image: a 7-record log (proj/tests.rs `rec`: seq i, 330 payload bytes (i*31 + j*7) % 251, sha256-chained ids),
# a first eval_blob with LogSummary (Full), 2 more records, a second eval_blob that STEPS by 2 -- the RUST writer.
# LogSummary = count u64 || payload bytes u64 || LOG fold u64 (LE): here 9 || 2970 || 6344481284825166345.
# Each reader prints `proj status=0 n=<records> root=<FNV-1a 64 of the LogSummary IT derives from the log> memo=<OUTB value>`.
#   oracle.py --proj: proj status=0 n=9 root=-9190210101691969827 memo=-9190210101691969827
n=9
root=-9190210101691969827
memo=-9190210101691969827
